  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto has expressed an intent to secure 70 percent of revenue from mining operations for the Indonesian state. In response to this directive, Coordinating Minister for Downstreaming and Energy Transition Bahlil Lahadalia has been tasked with preparing formal policy options to achieve the target. The initiative has prompted discussions regarding existing royalty structures within the mineral and coal sectors. While the government explores methods to increase state intake, the plan has garnered support from the House of Representatives as well as mining associations in Morowali. The discussions reflect broader efforts by the administration to maximize the economic benefits derived from the nation's natural resources. Previous reporting indicated that the administration is also aligning internal security measures, including the appointment of new police leadership, to support the government's national priorities and administrative stability.",
